  "comment": "PHASE 5 CLIP-SPLIT. The Intro Orchestrator (app/intro_orchestrator.cpp defaultIntroBeats) carves this single timeline into NAMED CLIP BEATS, with bounded interactive space-combat windows occupying the GAPS between them: cine.flight [0..20] -> play.dodge -> cine.reveal [20..30] -> cine.charge [30..36] -> play.dogfight (climax) -> cine.outcome. The outcome beat is OUTCOME-SELECTED: SHOT_DOWN plays [36..66] (the kill -> smash-to-black -> ESCAPE FROM LAB ZERO + SIX MONTHS LATER); ESCAPED plays [66..80] (you slip the kill-box, a glancing hit drains the antimatter, the ion-pulse drive ignites -> hands off to the Phase-6 atmo descent). Every authored span reads as a self-contained beat (camera framing, FX, titles). The capital ship resolves blob->detailed via a scale/distance ramp + an emissive ramp (emissiveFrom -> emissive) so it emerges as a lit, menacing hull instead of popping from a flat blob.",

